QAC_042,Factual,Medium,Constitutional,What are the grounds on which the office of President becomes vacant?,Article 38 of the Constitution lists the grounds on which the office of President shall become vacant: (a) upon death; (b) resignation addressed to the Speaker; (c) ceasing to be a citizen of Sri Lanka; (d) failure of the President-elect to assume office within two weeks; (e) removal from office; or (f) a Supreme Court determination that the President's election was void.,Article 38,Art. 38: (1) The office of President shall become vacant  office by President (a) upon his death; (b) if he resigns his office by a writing under his hand addressed to the Speaker; (c) if he ceases to be a cit,LEGAL_EXPERT_1 (Human-Annotated),2026-05-04,,,,,,,
