QAC_061,Factual,Medium,Constitutional,What are the qualifications to be registered as an elector?,"Article 88 provides that every person, unless disqualified as provided, shall be qualified to be an elector at the election of the President and Members of Parliament and to vote at any Referendum, provided that their name is entered in the appropriate register of electors. Article 89(b) further provides that no person shall be qualified to be an elector if they have not attained the age of eighteen years on the qualifying date specified by law. Article 88 thus sets the general entitlement and Article 89 sets the disqualifications, including the minimum voting age.","Article 88, Article 89","Art. 88: Every person shall, unless disqualified as elector hereinafter provided, be qualified to be an elector at the election of the President and of the Members of Parliament or to vote at any Referendum: P || Art. 89: No person shall be qualified to be an elector to be an elector at an election of the President, or of the Members of Parliament or to vote at any Referendum, if he is subject to any of the following d",LEGAL_EXPERT_1 (Human-Annotated),2026-05-04,,,,,,,
