QAC_230,Interpretive,Hard,Constitutional,How does Article 4 distribute governmental powers among the organs of state?,"Article 4 distributes sovereignty by assigning each power to a distinct organ: legislative power to Parliament (and the People at a Referendum), executive power to the President, judicial power to courts created by Parliament, and the franchise to citizens. This reflects a constitutional framework of separated but coordinated powers all derived from the sovereignty of the People under Article 3.","Article 3, Article 4","Art. 3: In the Republic of Sri Lanka sovereignty is Sovereignty in the People and is inalienable. Sovereignty includes the of the People powers of government, fundamental rights and the franchise. || Art. 4: The Sovereignty of the People shall be exercised Exercise of Sovereignty and enjoyed in the following manner: (a) the legislative power of the People shall be exercised by Parliament, consisting of el",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
