QAC_234,Interpretive,Medium,Constitutional,Can language qualifications legally be required for public employment under the Constitution?,Article 12(2) includes a proviso that it shall be lawful to require a person to acquire within a reasonable time sufficient knowledge of any language as a qualification for a post requiring the use of that language. This is an express constitutional exception to the prohibition on discrimination by language.,Article 12,"Art. 12: (1) All persons are equal before the law and are equality entitled to the equal protection of the law. (2) No citizen shall be discriminated against on the grounds of race, religion, language, caste,",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_235,Factual,Medium,Constitutional,What constitutional protections exist regarding access to public places?,"Article 12(3) provides that no person shall be subject to any disability, liability, restriction or condition with regard to access to shops, public restaurants, hotels, places of public entertainment, and places of public worship of his own religion on the grounds of race, religion, language, caste or sex.",Article 12,"Art. 12: (1) All persons are equal before the law and are equality entitled to the equal protection of the law. (2) No citizen shall be discriminated against on the grounds of race, religion, language, caste,",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_236,Factual,Easy,Constitutional,"Does the Constitution allow special legislative provisions for women, children, or disabled persons?","Article 12(4) expressly provides that nothing in the article shall prevent special provision being made by law for the advancement of women, children or disabled persons.",Article 12,"Art. 12: (1) All persons are equal before the law and are equality entitled to the equal protection of the law. (2) No citizen shall be discriminated against on the grounds of race, religion, language, caste,",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_237,Interpretive,Easy,Constitutional,A public institution rejects an applicant solely on grounds of caste. Which constitutional right may be violated?,Article 12(2) prohibits discrimination against any citizen on grounds that include caste. A public institution rejecting an applicant solely on grounds of caste would constitute discrimination contrary to Article 12(2). The applicant could invoke the Supreme Court's fundamental rights jurisdiction under Article 126 to seek redress.,"Article 12, Article 126","Art. 12: (1) All persons are equal before the law and are equality entitled to the equal protection of the law. (2) No citizen shall be discriminated against on the grounds of race, religion, language, caste, || Art. 126: (1) The Supreme Court shall have sole and rights exclusive jurisdiction to hear and determine any question jurisdiction and its relating to the infringement or imminent infringement by exercise execut",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_238,Interpretive,Medium,Constitutional,How does Article 12 balance the right to equality with language requirements in public employment?,"Article 12(1) guarantees equal protection of the law for all persons. Article 12(2) prohibits discrimination on grounds including language, but its proviso permits requiring acquisition of sufficient language knowledge as a qualification for posts that require use of that language. This balances equality with the practical needs of linguistic administration.",Article 12,"Art. 12: (1) All persons are equal before the law and are equality entitled to the equal protection of the law. (2) No citizen shall be discriminated against on the grounds of race, religion, language, caste,",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_239,Interpretive,Medium,Constitutional,Can affirmative action programmes for women or disabled persons be constitutionally valid under Article 12?,"Yes. Article 12(4) expressly provides that nothing in Article 12 shall prevent special provision being made by law for the advancement of women, children or disabled persons. Parliament may therefore enact laws making such special provision without violating the equality guarantee in Article 12(1).",Article 12,"Art. 12: (1) All persons are equal before the law and are equality entitled to the equal protection of the law. (2) No citizen shall be discriminated against on the grounds of race, religion, language, caste,",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_240,Factual,Easy,Constitutional,What right does an arrested person have immediately upon arrest?,"Article 13(1) provides that no person shall be arrested except according to procedure established by law, and any person arrested shall be informed of the reason for his arrest.",Article 13,"Art. 13: (1) No person shall be arrested except according Freedom from to procedure established by law. Any person arrested shall arbitrary arrest, be informed of the reason for his arrest. detention and punis",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_241,Factual,Medium,Constitutional,When must a person detained or held in custody be brought before a judge?,"Article 13(2) provides that every person held in custody, detained or otherwise deprived of personal liberty shall be brought before the judge of the nearest competent court according to procedure established by law and shall not be further held in custody, detained or deprived of personal liberty except upon and in terms of the order of such judge.",Article 13,"Art. 13: (1) No person shall be arrested except according Freedom from to procedure established by law. Any person arrested shall arbitrary arrest, be informed of the reason for his arrest. detention and punis",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_242,Factual,Medium,Constitutional,What rights does an accused person have during trial under the Constitution?,Article 13(3) provides that any person charged with an offence shall be entitled to be heard in person or by an attorney-at-law at a fair trial by a competent court.,Article 13,"Art. 13: (1) No person shall be arrested except according Freedom from to procedure established by law. Any person arrested shall arbitrary arrest, be informed of the reason for his arrest. detention and punis",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_243,Factual,Medium,Constitutional,Can punishment be imposed on a person without an order of a competent court?,"Article 13(4) provides that no person shall be punished with death or imprisonment except by order of a competent court. The article further provides that the arrest, holding in custody, detention or other deprivation of personal liberty of a person pending investigation or trial shall not constitute punishment.",Article 13,"Art. 13: (1) No person shall be arrested except according Freedom from to procedure established by law. Any person arrested shall arbitrary arrest, be informed of the reason for his arrest. detention and punis",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_244,Factual,Medium,Constitutional,Can a minimum penalty be imposed for an offence under the Constitution?,"Article 13(6) provides that it shall not be a contravention of Article 13 to require the imposition of a minimum penalty for an offence, provided that such penalty does not exceed the maximum penalty prescribed for such offence at the time the offence was committed. Parliament may therefore enact laws imposing minimum penalties subject to this constitutional limitation. (Article 13(7) deals separately with deprivation of liberty under removal or deportation orders, which is also declared not to constitute a contravention of Article 13.)",Article 13,"Art. 13: (6) No person shall be held guilty of an offence on account of any act or omission which did not, at the time of such act or omission, constitute such an offence and no penalty shall be imposed for an",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_245,Factual,Medium,Constitutional,What constitutional safeguards exist against arbitrary arrest and detention?,"Article 13 provides a set of safeguards: (1) no arrest except by procedure established by law, with reasons given; (2) prompt production before a judge; (3) right to a fair trial by a competent court; (4) no punishment except by court order; (5) no preventive detention without judicial review; and (6) no retrospective criminal penalties.",Article 13,"Art. 13: (1) No person shall be arrested except according Freedom from to procedure established by law. Any person arrested shall arbitrary arrest, be informed of the reason for his arrest. detention and punis",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_246,Interpretive,Medium,Constitutional,A suspect is denied legal representation during trial. Which constitutional provision may apply?,"Article 13(3) provides that any person charged with an offence shall be entitled to be heard in person or by an attorney-at-law at a fair trial by a competent court. Denial of legal representation would potentially constitute a violation of this constitutional right, which may be enforced under Article 126 through the Supreme Court's fundamental rights jurisdiction.","Article 13, Article 126","Art. 13: (1) No person shall be arrested except according Freedom from to procedure established by law. Any person arrested shall arbitrary arrest, be informed of the reason for his arrest. detention and punis || Art. 126: (1) The Supreme Court shall have sole and rights exclusive jurisdiction to hear and determine any question jurisdiction and its relating to the infringement or imminent infringement by exercise execut",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
QAC_247,Interpretive,Hard,Constitutional,Can preventive detention amount to punishment under Article 13?,"Article 13(4) expressly provides that the arrest, holding in custody, detention or other deprivation of personal liberty of a person pending investigation or trial shall not constitute punishment for the purposes of Article 13. However, Article 13(5) requires that any person deprived of personal liberty by arrest or detention shall be entitled to take proceedings before a competent court for the determination of the legality of the detention.",Article 13,"Art. 13: (1) No person shall be arrested except according Freedom from to procedure established by law. Any person arrested shall arbitrary arrest, be informed of the reason for his arrest. detention and punis",AI-Generated (Unreviewed),2026-05-18,,,,,,,
