ABS_016,factual,easy,Constitutional Law,What is the minimum age required to vote in a Sri Lankan general election?,Article 89(b) of the Constitution provides that no person shall be qualified to be an elector at an election of the President or Members of Parliament if they have not attained the age of eighteen years on the qualifying date specified by law. The minimum voting age is therefore eighteen years.,Article 89,"Art. 89: No person shall be qualified to be an elector to be an elector at an election of the President, or of the Members of Par || Art. 89: (j) if the period of his disqualification imposed under 58[Article 116 or Article 111C, as the case may be] has not elap",ABSTENTION_EVAL,2026-05-26,,,,,,,
ABS_017,factual,medium,Constitutional Law,What are the functions and powers of the Attorney General of Sri Lanka?,"Article 61E of the Constitution provides that the President shall appoint the Attorney-General on the approval of the Constitutional Council. Article 134(1) provides that the Attorney-General shall be notified and shall have the right to be heard in all proceedings in the Supreme Court in the exercise of its jurisdiction under Articles 120, 121, 122, 125, 126, and 129(1). These provisions establish the constitutional basis for the appointment and right of audience of the Attorney-General before the Supreme Court.","Article 61E, Article 134","Art. 61E: The President shall appoint - by the President (a) the Heads of the Army, the Navy and the Air Force; and (b) 46[on the  || Art. 134: (1) The Attorney-General shall be noticed and Right to be have the right to be heard in all proceedings in the heard by ",ABSTENTION_EVAL,2026-05-26,,,,,,,
