ABS_020,factual,medium,Constitutional Law,How is the Cabinet of Ministers of Sri Lanka constituted and who appoints Ministers?,"Article 44(1) of the Constitution provides that the President shall appoint from among Members of Parliament Ministers of the Cabinet of Ministers to be in charge of such subjects and functions as the President shall assign to them. Article 43(1) further provides that there shall be a Cabinet of Ministers charged with the direction and control of the Government, which shall be collectively responsible and answerable to Parliament.","Article 43, Article 44","Art. 44: (1) The President shall, in consultation with and their the Prime Minister, where he considers such consultation subject || Art. 44: The President shall, in consultation with and their the Prime Minister, where he considers such consultation subjects an",ABSTENTION_EVAL,2026-05-26,,,,,,,
